<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(3.4 Box Plot Analysis  Box plots were constructed to visualise the inter-quartile ranges and outliers for each feature across the three driving classes. The plots confirm that the AGGRESSIVE class exhibits greater variability \(wider IQR\) in AccX, AccY, and AccZ compared to NORMAL and SLOW classes, providing early evidence that acceleration magnitude and variability are discriminative features. )/E(3.4 Box Plot Analysis  Box plots were constructed to visualise the inter-quartile ranges and outliers for each feature across the three driving classes. The plots confirm that the AGGRESSIVE class exhibits greater variability \(wider IQR\) in AccX, AccY, and AccZ compared to NORMAL and SLOW classes, providing early evidence that acceleration magnitude and variability are discriminative features. )/K[6]/P 360 0 R/Pg 12 0 R>>
