403 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(3.5 Correlation Analysis  A Pearson correlation matrix was computed for the six sensor features. The analysis reveals that features are largely uncorrelated with each other \(most correlations below 0.3\), with the strongest correlation observed between AccX and GyroZ \(\2120.32\). This low inter-feature correlation is beneficial, as it indicates that each sensor axis provides unique information, and multicollinearity is not a concern for tree-based models. )/E(3.5 Correlation Analysis  A Pearson correlation matrix was computed for the six sensor features. The analysis reveals that features are largely uncorrelated with each other \(most correlations below 0.3\), with the strongest correlation observed between AccX and GyroZ \(\2120.32\). This low inter-feature correlation is beneficial, as it indicates that each sensor axis provides unique information, and multicollinearity is not a concern for tree-based models. )/K[6]/P 396 0 R/Pg 13 0 R>>
endobj

