<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(3.6 Time-Series Pattern Analysis  A sample of 200 consecutive records from each class was plotted as a time series to observe the temporal characteristics of each driving style. The plots clearly demonstrate that AGGRESSIVE driving produces high-amplitude, erratic oscillations in acceleration, while SLOW driving shows a noticeably wider spread in accelerometer readings, particularly in AccY and AccZ, reflecting the erratic nature of aggressive driving.)/E(3.6 Time-Series Pattern Analysis  A sample of 200 consecutive records from each class was plotted as a time series to observe the temporal characteristics of each driving style. The plots clearly demonstrate that AGGRESSIVE driving produces high-amplitude, erratic oscillations in acceleration, while SLOW driving shows a noticeably wider spread in accelerometer readings, particularly in AccY and AccZ, reflecting the erratic nature of aggressive driving.)/K[6]/P 432 0 R/Pg 14 0 R>>
