527 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(CHAPTER 4: DATA MODELLING  4.1 Feature Engineering  Feature engineering is a critical step that transforms raw sensor readings into a richer representation that enables machine learning models to detect subtle patterns. A total of 32 new features were engineered from the original 6 sensor measurements, bringing the total feature count to 38. The following categories of features were created: )/E(CHAPTER 4: DATA MODELLING  4.1 Feature Engineering  Feature engineering is a critical step that transforms raw sensor readings into a richer representation that enables machine learning models to detect subtle patterns. A total of 32 new features were engineered from the original 6 sensor measurements, bringing the total feature count to 38. The following categories of features were created: )/K[4]/P 523 0 R/Pg 16 0 R>>
endobj

528 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Magnitude Features \(3 features\): Three magnitude features were computed as the Euclidean norm across axes: AccMagnitude, GyroMagnitude, and JerkMagnitude. These scalar measures capture the overall intensity of motion irrespective of direction. )/E(Magnitude Features \(3 features\): Three magnitude features were computed as the Euclidean norm across axes: AccMagnitude, GyroMagnitude, and JerkMagnitude. These scalar measures capture the overall intensity of motion irrespective of direction. )/K[5]/P 523 0 R/Pg 16 0 R>>
endobj

529 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Rolling Window Statistics \(12 features\): A 30-sample sliding window was applied to compute rolling means and rolling standard deviations for accelerometer readings, and rolling means and rolling maxima for jerk values. These features capture the local temporal dynamics of each driving segment. )/E(Rolling Window Statistics \(12 features\): A 30-sample sliding window was applied to compute rolling means and rolling standard deviations for accelerometer readings, and rolling means and rolling maxima for jerk values. These features capture the local temporal dynamics of each driving segment. )/K[6]/P 523 0 R/Pg 16 0 R>>
endobj

530 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/H2/T(Statistical Aggregation Features \(7 features\): Additional features including squared accelerations \(AccX_var, AccY_var, AccZ_var\), absolute accelerations \(AbsAccX, AbsAccY, AbsAccZ\), and Acc_Energy were computed to capture the energycontent of the sensor signals. )/E(Statistical Aggregation Features \(7 features\): Additional features including squared accelerations \(AccX_var, AccY_var, AccZ_var\), absolute accelerations \(AbsAccX, AbsAccY, AbsAccZ\), and Acc_Energy were computed to capture the energycontent of the sensor signals. )/K[7]/P 523 0 R/Pg 16 0 R>>
endobj

